            <div xml:id="d536">

                <pb facs="0560" n="548" sameAs="frus:frus1937v01/pg548"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">852.2221 Dahl, Harold/61: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Seville</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Bay</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the
                            Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Seville</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-09-14T10:00:00+01:00">September 14, 1937—10
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received September 14—6:34 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Referring to your [<hi rendition="#italic">my?</hi>] telegram of September 13
                        [<hi rendition="#italic">12?</hi>], 10 a.m. Letter just received from
                    General Queipo de Llano states that General Franco declares that Dahl has not
                    been condemned to death but has been placed on the list of prisoners to be
                    exchanged.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Bay</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
